<configuration name="signalwire.conf" description="SignalWire">
  <settings>
    <!--
        This file is not shipped by the lab by default - the package installs
        one, but ./conf is bind-mounted over /etc/freeswitch, which masks it.
        The module has working built-in defaults, so its absence is normally
        harmless.

        It is here to override the STUN server. mod_signalwire does two
        separate STUN lookups - one to complete adoption, and one in
        mod_signalwire_state_configure() to report its SIP endpoint to
        SignalWire. Unlike the generic `stun` API, both bind to a specific
        local IP and a fixed port from 6050 upwards, which on Docker Desktop
        behaves differently from an ephemeral bind.

        Observed on Docker Desktop, all with `fs_cli -x "stun <server>"`
        succeeding 3/3 against every one of them:

          stun.freeswitch.org      adoption times out
          stun.l.google.com:19302  adoption works, configure times out in a
                                   4-second retry loop:
                                     SignalWire configure failed: stun [...] Timeout
          stun.cloudflare.com:3478 both succeed

        So the generic STUN API is not a valid test of whether the module will
        work - only the module's own bind pattern is. Cloudflare is used
        because it is the only one observed to satisfy both call sites.

        Format is host:port.
    -->
    <param name="stun-server" value="stun.cloudflare.com:3478"/>

    <!-- on/off/file-path -->
    <!--<param name="kslog" value="on"/>-->
    <!--<param name="blade-bootstrap" value="blade://switchblade:2100"/>-->
    <!--<param name="adoption-service" value="https://adopt.signalwire.com/adoption"/>-->
    <!-- override dialplan context for calls on connector -->
    <!--<param name="override-context" value="signalwire"/>-->
  </settings>
</configuration>
